\DOC ACCUMULATOR_ASSUM_LIST

\TYPE {ACCUMULATOR_ASSUM_LIST : ((thm list) -> tactic) -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
{ACCUMULATOR_ASSUM_LIST ttac} applies the tactic-producing function {ttac} to a
selected sublist of the goal's assumptions, supplied as theorems, leaving the
assumption list itself untouched.

\DESCRIBE
The argument {ttac : (thm list) -> tactic} receives the chosen assumptions as
theorems, and the tactic it returns is what acts on the goal. The assumptions
handed to {ttac} are not all of {A} but a subset of them (in the observed
traces, equations relating word values, carries and sums), and they remain in
the assumption list afterwards. Every observed trace yields a single subgoal
with {A} unchanged, only the conclusion being altered, in whatever way the
tactic built by {ttac} dictates. Typically {ttac} was a function that conjoins
the supplied theorems (after transforming them with a derived rule) and
discharges the result with {MP_TAC}:
{
       A ?- t
   ============== ACCUMULATOR_ASSUM_LIST ttac
    A ?- u ==> t
}
\noindent where {u} is a conjunction derived from the selected assumptions. One
trace instead used a {ttac} that rewrites, so the conclusion {t} was replaced
by a rewritten {t}.

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only this single-subgoal, conclusion-only behaviour,
always with the chosen assumptions still present.

\ENDDOC
